==English==
===Etymology===
1670s, from {{etyl|la}} {{term|subtrahendus|lang=la}} {{term|numerus||number to be subtracted|lang=la}}, form of {{term|subtraho|subtrahō|I pull out from under, I subtract|lang=la}} (English {{term|subtract|lang=en}}).<ref>{{R:Online Etymology Dictionary}}</ref>

Surface analysis is {{suffix|subtract|end|t2=patient (recipient) of action}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{arithmetic}} A number or quantity to be subtracted from another.
#: ''In the subtraction 10 &minus; 4, 4 is the subtrahend.''

